etchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">det</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">[</mo><mtable columnalign=\"center\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>\u22c5</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>\u2212</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>\u22c5</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>\u2260</mo><mn>0.</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Now, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. </p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's now check our statements.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem. </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is false since, according to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"97\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D431 TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D7CE TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assi